["<task-notification>\n<task-id>aa8c10205adf919fe</task-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/tasks/aa8c10205adf919fe.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix health orb pickup and hint\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>There's no real bug beyond the full-HP rule. When the player is hurt, orbs are collected; at full HP they now dim and show \"满血,留着\" when the player is close. All work is in the `fix/health-orb` worktree; nothing was merged.\n\n**Root cause.** I traced it from the bottom up and found nothing that stops a hurt player from picking up an orb:\n- **HP and max HP stay in sync.** Every stat change, whatever its source (item, `equip:*`, talent, boon), updates max HP and adjusts current HP. Raising max HP heals by the same amount; lowering it clamps HP to the new max. So HP can't get stuck above max HP. The `fury` talent's −10% max HP clamps HP and does not trap it.\n- **PickupRange:** the base is 3.5, and item/equipment/talent bonuses widen the magnet.\n- **Phases:** after a room is cleared the game stays in the Fight phase until the player takes the exit, so orbs stay collectible. Orbs are cleared on Hub/Result, or destroyed with the room when it is rebuilt.\n- **Placement:** drop points avoid the bounds of pillars and props. If no free spot is found, the orb lands on the enemy's own position, which the player can reach.\n\nNew EditMode tests pin this: a hurt player with flat/percent max HP and pickup-range sources wants the orb, gets pulled and collects it; 400 random max HP changes never leave HP above max; the `fury` cut at full HP clamps HP, then one hit makes the orb wanted.\n\n**Live evidence.** The bot log now ends each run with a `[Pickups]` line. Final gate run: `collected=1/0/1`, `ignoredAtFullHp=0`, `expiredHurt=0`. The orbs it didn't collect were left behind when it took the exit (`leftInRoom=2/3/0`); the bot walks straight to the exit and doesn't go for orbs.\n\n**Commits**\n- `6444c6c` adds the regression tests and the per-run `[Pickups]` log line.\n- `6d97a18` fixes my own log line: it printed twice per run (on Result and again on Hub) and didn't count orbs destroyed with a room.\n- `e86c5a7` is the change you asked for. The dim/hint decision is pure logic in `PickupRules.cs`, with tests. At full HP the orb fades to a grey-green with a faint glow and no sparkle. \"满血,留着\" (NotoSansSC, with a dark shadow for contrast on the pale floor) appears only within 4 m. Fades take 0.3 s on unscaled time and don't touch `Time.timeScale`. Once the player is hurt, the orb brightens and the magnet works again.\n  - It also stops the screenshot-only demo orbs from counting in the tally. That piece is logging rather than UX, so this commit isn't strictly one concern.\n\n**Gates**\n- **EditMode:** 1221/1221 pass (1215 existing + 6 new).\n- **Bot:** `tools/run-bot-watched.sh &lt;copy&gt; &lt;out&gt; 3 120 1200` printed `[BOT] finished runs=3 wins=3`. The only ERROR is the known frame-1 SearchDatabase `ArgumentOutOfRangeException`.\n- **Screenshot:** `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad/orb/shot7/png/pickup_showcase.png` shows the dimmed orb with a legible label next to a bright orb and a coin. A shot from the gameplay camera distance (earlier run, same hint style) is `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-youxun-project-game-agent-roguelite/7cf6507c-b688-43d0-9e91-b78620dd6a1f/scratchpad/orb/shot5/png/pickup_showcase_gameplay.png`.\n\n**Not verified, and other caveats**\n- **Screenshot workaround:** with `AGENT_SHOT_DIR` set, the bot sticks in the Hub in headless mode, because it waits for HUD captures that never run headless. The windowed launch stalled after licensing, probably because your editor is open on the main project. I got the screenshots by patching `HudShot.Busy` in the scratch copy only, not committed. That existing bug in the screenshot tooling is still there.\n- **Not seen in live play:** the hint fading in and out as a real player walks up at full HP. The showcase forces that state.\n- **Label offset in the close-up:** the label sits a little left of its orb because it turns to face the game camera, not the screenshot camera. In normal play it should be centred, but I haven't seen that.\n- **New test `.meta` files** use GUIDs I generated by hand.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>185957</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>103</tool_uses><duration_ms>1223446</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"]
